From 7ce7c58dcad9d87e4ef7b8be51f4a293818b7b6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TEX8 Wallet <engineering@tex8.app>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 10:35:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wallet: bound global gRPC range pool to four transport lanes

The adaptive wallet selected eight logical finite ranges, but every range
client reused the same process channel because the cache was keyed only by the
target. This collapsed the pool onto one physical HTTP/2/TCP transport. Current
CLI profiles measured 312 range clients as one created plus 311 reused channel
handles while block fetch dominated the end-to-end duration.

Keep one global downloader and the existing exact-range cache, but key its
process-wide channels by a bounded lane number and give every channel its local
gRPC subchannel pool, preventing gRPC Core from merging the four channel
objects back onto one physical TCP transport. Range slots reuse lanes zero
through three across successive, non-overlapping ranges. This does not create
per-wallet downloaders and never downloads one range twice. Four lanes are the
measured optimum in the retained D5/D6 transport evidence; eight or more were
slower.
